    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2023-competency-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.38";
    dc:description "Comparative molecular data can test parts of the ancestry claim. They cannot cleanly establish the broad cost contrast or that competency is automatically available to multicellular evolution.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compare phylogenetically reconstructed cellular sensing and action machinery with organism-level learning machinery, measuring whether multicellular lineages inherit rather than newly evolve each capacity and its energetic cost. Support requires ancestral cellular competencies to precede and reduce the evolutionary cost of developmental control.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'By default' and 'paid for' lack unique quantitative definitions.", "Cellular and organismal mechanisms overlap.", "Deep ancestral capabilities are reconstructed indirectly.";
